---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const translateGoalsResult = await translateGoals(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const designProjectResult = await designProject(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, translateGoalsResult.accepted);
const sequenceMilestonesResult = await sequenceMilestones(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, designProjectResult.accepted);
const adaptScaffoldingResult = await adaptScaffolding(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, sequenceMilestonesResult.accepted);
const introduceComplicationsResult = await introduceComplications(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, adaptScaffoldingResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { translateGoals: translateGoalsResult, designProject: designProjectResult, sequenceMilestones: sequenceMilestonesResult, adaptScaffolding: adaptScaffoldingResult, introduceComplications: introduceComplicationsResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...translateGoalsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...designProjectResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...sequenceMilestonesResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...adaptScaffoldingResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...introduceComplicationsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...translateGoalsResult.checks, ...designProjectResult.checks, ...sequenceMilestonesResult.checks, ...adaptScaffoldingResult.checks, ...introduceComplicationsResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — One learner misses a milestone: redistribute logistics without erasing individual evidence requirements. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (redistribute logistics without erasing individual evidence requirements.) through the existing stage result for ProjectLearningGoal; preserve exact source/version and the prior ProjectLearningGoal, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A required material becomes unavailable: propose an equivalent route preserving the learning goal. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (propose an equivalent route preserving the learning goal.) through the existing stage result for ProjectLearningGoal; preserve exact source/version and the prior ProjectLearningGoal, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — A group produces polished work with unclear authorship: request individual demonstrations. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (request individual demonstrations.) through the existing stage result for ProjectLearningGoal; preserve exact source/version and the prior ProjectLearningGoal, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A complication arrives near the deadline: validate remaining feasibility before release. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (validate remaining feasibility before release.) through the existing stage result for ProjectLearningGoal; preserve exact source/version and the prior ProjectLearningGoal, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — A learner uses a creative alternative: assess the competency rather than adherence to the sample solution. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (assess the competency rather than adherence to the sample solution.) through the existing stage result for ProjectLearningGoal; preserve exact source/version and the prior ProjectLearningGoal, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, translateGoals: translateGoalsResult, designProject: designProjectResult, sequenceMilestones: sequenceMilestonesResult, adaptScaffolding: adaptScaffoldingResult, introduceComplications: introduceComplicationsResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
